2. Excessive Database Metadata and Security Information Disclosure

Severity: Low
CVSS v3.1: 4.3
OWASP: A01:2021 – Broken Access Control
Category: Information Disclosure

Description

It was observed that the database account was able to access metadata information from system tables and catalog objects. The accessible information included database names, user accounts, roles, permissions, and security-related configuration details. Although access to certain system objects was restricted, the account could still enumerate valuable database structure and security information.

The exposed metadata may assist attackers in mapping the database environment, identifying privileged accounts, and understanding internal security architecture. Such information can be leveraged during further attack phases to identify high-value targets and potential privilege escalation opportunities.

Impact
Database structure disclosure.
User and role enumeration.
Facilitates targeted attacks.
Increases attack surface visibility.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement the principle of least privilege and restrict access to system catalog objects, metadata tables, and administrative views. Access to security-related information should only be granted to authorized administrators.

PoC
select * from master..sysusers
