3. Exposed RPC and NFS Services

Severity: Low
CVSS v3.1: 5.3
OWASP: A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration
Category: Network Exposure

Description

It was observed that RPCBind (Port 111/TCP) and NFS services (Port 2049/TCP) were exposed on the target host. Service enumeration identified active RPC services including mountd, nlockmgr, and NFS-related services.

These services are commonly targeted for reconnaissance and exploitation activities. Exposed RPC services can reveal information regarding exported file systems, service mappings, and network architecture.

Impact
Service enumeration.
Potential unauthorized file share discovery.
Increased attack surface.
Exposure of infrastructure details.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement network segmentation and firewall restrictions to limit access to RPC and NFS services. Disable unnecessary services and restrict exposure to trusted hosts only.

PoC
nmap -sV -Pn --script rpcinfo <target>
References
CIS Controls v8
NIST SP 800-53 CM-7
4. National Identification Numbers Stored and Accessible in Clear Text

Severity: Low
CVSS v3.1: 5.5
OWASP: A02:2021 – Cryptographic Failures
Category: Sensitive Data Exposure

Description

It was observed that national identification numbers were stored and returned in clear text format within database tables. Sample records included identifiers such as national IDs and government-issued identification numbers without masking or encryption.

The database account possessing highly restricted read permissions was able to retrieve these values directly from the database.

Impact
Exposure of sensitive personal information.
Increased privacy risk.
Regulatory compliance concerns.
Potential misuse of personal identifiers.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement encryption, masking, tokenization, or other data protection controls for sensitive identification numbers. Access should be limited to authorized business users only.

PoC
select top 100 * from PartyNationalID
