5. Password Expiration Policy Disabled

Severity: Informational
CVSS v3.1: 3.1
OWASP: A07:2021 – Identification and Authentication Failures
Category: Authentication Configuration

Description

It was observed that the system-wide password expiration policy was disabled. User account information showed that password expiration controls were not enforced.

Although Kerberos authentication was enabled, locally managed database accounts may remain active indefinitely without periodic credential rotation.

Impact
Long-lived credentials.
Increased risk from compromised passwords.
Reduced credential hygiene.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement periodic password expiration requirements for locally managed database accounts and service accounts where operationally feasible.

PoC
sp_configure "password policy"
