7. SSH Supports Legacy SHA-1 Cryptographic Algorithms

Severity: Informational
CVSS v3.1: 3.7
OWASP: A02:2021 – Cryptographic Failures
Category: Weak Cryptography

Description

It was observed that the SSH service supported SHA-1 based key exchange and cryptographic algorithms. Enumeration identified legacy Diffie-Hellman SHA-1 algorithms supported by the server.

SHA-1 is considered cryptographically weak and has been deprecated by industry standards.

Impact
Reduced cryptographic strength.
Potential future compatibility and security concerns.
Increased exposure to cryptographic attacks.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement modern cryptographic algorithms such as SHA-256 or SHA-512 based key exchange mechanisms and disable legacy SHA-1 algorithms.

PoC
nmap --script ssh2-enum-algos -p22 <target>
