9. Weak Account Lockout Configuration

Severity: Low
CVSS v3.1: 4.0
OWASP: A07:2021 – Identification and Authentication Failures
Category: Authentication Security

Description

It was observed that the maximum failed login threshold was configured as 32767. This effectively disables account lockout protection against repeated authentication attempts.

The absence of a practical lockout threshold increases susceptibility to password guessing and brute-force attacks against database accounts.

Impact
Increased brute-force attack risk.
Weak authentication controls.
Reduced protection against credential attacks.
Mitigation

It is recommended to implement a reasonable account lockout threshold, such as 5–10 failed login attempts, and configure monitoring for repeated authentication failures.

PoC
sp_configure "maximum failed logins"

Observed Result

maximum failed logins = 32767
